IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sumlma-member`

-- Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999 -- what the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members)
-- Regulations 2019 prescribe for the member: the eligibility age (reg 5, Act s 10(1)); the visas excluded from the former
-- temporary resident rules (reg 7, Act ss 20AA(2), 20H); the interest paid with a refund (reg 9); the KiwiSaver matters
-- (reg 20); the "prescribed period" for a transfer to my active account (reg 13, Act s 24NA(2)(c)); and which fund gets it
-- where more than one qualifies (reg 14, Act s 24NA(3)). A module beside sumlma-member.l4 in the same baseline; it IMPORTs
-- that module and changes none of it.
--
-- SEAT: the member (as in sumlma-member.l4).
--
-- Sources:
--   the Act, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00518.txt;
--   the Regulations, compilation F2025C00752 (Compilation No. 6, 25 July 2025) of F2019L01617, as deposited at
--   ../../../superannuation-unclaimed-money-and-lost-members-regulations-2019/registers/source-bundle/F2019L01617.txt, with the
--   formula of reg 9(5) from F2019L01617.formulas.md beside it.
--
-- The Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Regulations 1999 named in REQ-0086 were repealed; the 2019
-- Regulations are the ones in force (NOTES.md finding 12). Reg 8 (interest for periods ending on 30 June 2013, by the Treasury
-- bond rate) and Part 7 (public sector schemes) are not encoded. The CPI index numbers reg 9 uses are inputs: they are the
-- Australian Statistician's, not deposited.

§ `Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Regulations 2019 -- what they prescribe for me`

§§ `reg 5 -- my eligibility age`

-- Act s 10(1): eligibility age is 65 for a man and 60 for a woman, "or, if another age is prescribed by the regulations, the
-- age so prescribed". Reg 5: "For the purposes of paragraphs 10(1)(a) and (b) of the Act, the prescribed age for a member of a
-- fund is the greater of: (a) 65 years; and (b) if the governing rules of the fund specify that a benefit is payable to a
-- member only at a specified age that is greater than 65 years--that age." So the prescribed age replaces both the man's 65 and
-- the woman's 60, and what the fund knows of my sex no longer matters (NOTES.md finding 13).
@export What is my eligibility age under the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Regulations (reg 5)?
GIVEN `the age my fund's rules pay benefits at, if over 65` IS A NUMBER @desc If your fund's rules say a benefit is payable to you only at a specified age greater than 65, that age; otherwise 0
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my eligibility age under the Regulations` MEANS
    max 65 `the age my fund's rules pay benefits at, if over 65`

-- Act s 12(1), with reg 5's age in place of s 10(1)'s 65 and 60.
@export Is the money my super fund holds for me "unclaimed money" (s 12(1)), with the eligibility age the Regulations prescribe, and must my fund try to contact me (s 13)?
GIVEN `the age my fund's rules pay benefits at, if over 65` IS A NUMBER @desc If your fund's rules say a benefit is payable to you only at a specified age greater than 65, that age; otherwise 0
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in complete years, as your fund knows it or has determined it under s 10(2)(b) if it does not know your date of birth
      `months since an amount was received` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months since your fund last received any amount for you (a contribution, a rollover or anything else)
      `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for a defined benefits scheme: whether any benefit has accrued for you within the last 2 years (answer no for an ordinary accumulation account)
      `years since last contact` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete years since your fund last had contact with you
      `my fund cannot reach me after reasonable efforts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fund, after making reasonable efforts since those 5 years ended, has been unable to contact you again
GIVETH AN `Is my super unclaimed money`
`Is my super unclaimed money, at the prescribed age` MEANS
    IF      `my age` AT LEAST (`What is my eligibility age under the Regulations` `the age my fund's rules pay benefits at, if over 65`)
        AND `nothing received or accrued for me within the last 2 years` `months since an amount was received` `a defined benefit accrued within 2 years`
        AND `years since last contact` AT LEAST 5
    THEN IF `my fund cannot reach me after reasonable efforts`
         THEN `yes: it is unclaimed money (s 12(1)), and my fund must pay it to the Commissioner (s 17(1))`
         ELSE `not yet: but my fund must make reasonable efforts to contact me (s 13(1))`
    ELSE `no: it is not unclaimed money under s 12(1)`

§§ `reg 7 -- the visas excluded from the former temporary resident rules (if you held a temporary visa)`

-- Reg 7: "For the purposes of subsection 20AA(2) and subparagraphs 20H(1)(a)(ii) and 20H(2)(b)(iii) of the Act, the following
-- visas, as described in Schedule 2 to the Migration Regulations 1994, are prescribed: (a) Subclass 405 (Investor Retirement)
-- visa; (b) Subclass 410 (Retirement) visa."
DECLARE `The temporary visa I held` IS ONE OF
    `a Subclass 405 (Investor Retirement) visa`
    `a Subclass 410 (Retirement) visa`
    `another temporary visa`

GIVEN `the visa` IS A `The temporary visa I held`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the visa is prescribed by reg 7` IF
    NOT (`the visa` EQUALS `another temporary visa`)

@export I held a temporary visa and have left Australia. Am I a "former temporary resident" (s 20AA), given the visas the Regulations exclude?
GIVEN `my temporary visa has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a temporary visa under the Migration Act 1958 that has now ceased to be in effect
      `the visa` IS A `The temporary visa I held` @desc Which temporary visa you held: a Subclass 405 (Investor Retirement), a Subclass 410 (Retirement), or another
      `I left Australia after it began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you left Australia after you started to hold that visa
      `months since the later event` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have passed since the later of the visa ceasing and your leaving Australia
      `I now hold an Australian visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you now hold a temporary or permanent visa under the Migration Act 1958
      `I am an Australian or New Zealand citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen or a New Zealand citizen
      `my permanent visa application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a valid application for a permanent visa that has not been finally determined
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a former temporary resident, given the visas reg 7 excludes` IF
    `Am I a former temporary resident` `my temporary visa has ceased` (`the visa is prescribed by reg 7` `the visa`) `I left Australia after it began` `months since the later event` `I now hold an Australian visa` `I am an Australian or New Zealand citizen` `my permanent visa application is pending`

§§ `reg 20 -- paying my money to a KiwiSaver scheme (if you have moved to New Zealand)`

-- Reg 20(2): "The following matters are prescribed: (a) the person has emigrated permanently to New Zealand; (b) the person has
-- given the Commissioner proof of residence at an address in New Zealand following the person's emigration to New Zealand;
-- (c) the person has opened a KiwiSaver scheme account; (d) the Commissioner has been given sufficient details of the
-- KiwiSaver scheme and the account number to which the amount is to be paid; (e) the KiwiSaver scheme provider will accept
-- the amount; (f) the taxable component of any superannuation benefit that is paid by the Commissioner would not consist of, or
-- include, an amount that is an element untaxed in the fund." These are the "matters (if any) prescribed by the regulations"
-- of Act ss 17(2)(aa)(iii), 20H(2)(ba), 20QF(2)(aa)(iii), 21E(2)(aa)(iii), 22B(2)(aa)(iii), 24G(2)(aa)(iii).
@export I have directed the ATO to pay my super to a KiwiSaver scheme. Are the matters the Regulations prescribe met (reg 20)?
GIVEN `I have emigrated permanently to New Zealand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have emigrated permanently to New Zealand
      `I have given the Commissioner proof of my New Zealand address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Commissioner proof of residence at an address in New Zealand after emigrating
      `I have opened a KiwiSaver account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opened a KiwiSaver scheme account
      `the Commissioner has the scheme and account details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has been given enough details of the KiwiSaver scheme and the account number to pay into
      `the provider will accept it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the KiwiSaver scheme provider will accept the amount
      `the payment would include an untaxed element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the taxable component of the payment would consist of or include an element untaxed in the fund (for example from some public sector schemes)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the KiwiSaver matters prescribed by reg 20 met` IF
        `I have emigrated permanently to New Zealand`
    AND `I have given the Commissioner proof of my New Zealand address`
    AND `I have opened a KiwiSaver account`
    AND `the Commissioner has the scheme and account details`
    AND `the provider will accept it`
    AND (NOT `the payment would include an untaxed element`)

§§ `reg 9 -- how much interest comes with my refund`

-- Reg 9(1): applies to an amount a provider was required to pay (or paid) under ss 17, 20F, 20QD, 21C, 22 or 24E that the
-- Commissioner pays out under ss 17(2), 20H(2), 20QF(2), 21E(2), 22B(2), 24G(2) or 24NA(2) or (3). (2): not to an amount
-- refunded to a provider or a s 65AA(2) SGAA amount. (3): the interest period starts on the later of 1 July 2013 and the day the
-- provider was required to pay (or paid) the Commissioner, and ends on the third day after the Commissioner last authorised the
-- payment. (4): "adding together the interest for each financial year during the interest period". (5): for each financial
-- year, the formula (F2019L01617.formulas.md): Amount x Days interest payable x Interest rate / Days in the financial year,
-- "rounding the result to the nearest cent (with 0.5 cents being rounded up)", where "amount means the unclaimed amount plus the
-- interest (if any) worked out for each earlier financial year"; "interest rate, for a financial year, means: (a) the
-- percentage change in the CPI number between the 2 March quarters most recently published before the first day of the
-- financial year (rounded up to 4 decimal places); or (b) if that percentage change is less than 0%--0%."
-- "Rounded up to 4 decimal places" is read as rounding upwards (a ceiling) at the fourth place (NOTES.md finding 14); the
-- percentage is applied as a rate (3.5% as 0.035).
@export What is the reg 9 interest rate for a financial year, as a percentage, from the CPI numbers for the two March quarters published before it began?
GIVEN `the CPI number for the earlier March quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number (weighted average of the 8 capital cities) for the March quarter a year before the later one, as published by the ABS
      `the CPI number for the later March quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number for the most recent March quarter published before the financial year began
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the reg 9 interest rate` MEANS
    max 0 ((CEILING (`the change` TIMES 10000)) DIVIDED BY 10000)
    WHERE
        `the change` MEANS ((`the CPI number for the later March quarter` DIVIDED BY `the CPI number for the earlier March quarter`) MINUS 1) TIMES 100

@export How much interest does the ATO add to my refund for one financial year of the interest period (reg 9(5))?
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the ATO holds for you, plus any interest already worked out for earlier financial years of the interest period, in dollars
      `days interest payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of this financial year fall in the interest period
      `days in the financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the financial year has (365, or 366 if it includes 29 February)
      `the CPI number for the earlier March quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number (weighted average of the 8 capital cities) for the March quarter a year before the later one, as published by the ABS
      `the CPI number for the later March quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The All Groups CPI number for the most recent March quarter published before the financial year began
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much interest for one financial year` MEANS
    (FLOOR (((`the amount` TIMES `days interest payable` TIMES (`What is the reg 9 interest rate` `the CPI number for the earlier March quarter` `the CPI number for the later March quarter` DIVIDED BY 100)) DIVIDED BY `days in the financial year`) TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `regs 13, 14 -- moving my money into my active account (if the ATO holds super for you)`

-- Act s 24NA(2)(c): the fund "has received an amount in respect of the person during the prescribed period". Reg 13: "the
-- prescribed period is the period: (a) beginning on the first day of the financial year immediately preceding the financial
-- year in which the payment by the Commissioner under subsection 24NA(2) of the Act is made; and (b) ending on the day
-- immediately preceding the day on which the payment ... is made."
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the financial year before the one containing` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 7
    THEN Date 1 7 (DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1)
    ELSE Date 1 7 (DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 2)

@export Did my active fund receive an amount for me in the period the Regulations prescribe for a transfer (reg 13, s 24NA(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the day the ATO pays` IS A DATE @desc The day the Commissioner makes (or would make) the payment into your active account
      `the day my fund last received an amount for me` IS A DATE @desc The last day your active fund received an amount for you (a contribution or rollover) before that day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my fund receive an amount in the prescribed period` IF
        `the day my fund last received an amount for me` AT LEAST (`the first day of the financial year before the one containing` `the day the ATO pays`)
    AND `the day my fund last received an amount for me` LESS THAN `the day the ATO pays`

-- Reg 14(2): where more than one fund meets s 24NA(2)(b) to (e), the Commissioner pays "(a) if the Commissioner has made any
-- payment under subsection 17(2) or section 20H, 20QF, 21E, 22B, 24G or 24NA of the Act to an eligible fund for crediting to
-- the person during the financial year in which the Commissioner pays ...: (i) if there is only one such eligible fund--that
-- eligible fund; or (ii) if there is more than one such eligible fund--the eligible fund to which the Commissioner has most
-- recently made any of those payments; (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply--the eligible fund that most recently received an
-- amount in respect of the person during the period consisting of: (i) the financial year in which the Commissioner pays ...;
-- and (ii) the immediately preceding financial year; (c) if paragraphs (a) and (b) do not apply--the eligible fund that holds
-- the largest account balance for the person at the end of the last completed financial year ...; (d) if paragraphs (a), (b)
-- and (c) do not apply--the eligible fund determined by the Commissioner."
DECLARE `Which of my funds the ATO must pay` IS ONE OF
    `the fund the Commissioner has already paid for me this financial year (the most recently paid, if more than one) (reg 14(2)(a))`
    `the fund that most recently received an amount for me this financial year or last (reg 14(2)(b))`
    `the fund with the largest balance for me at the end of the last completed financial year (reg 14(2)(c))`
    `the fund the Commissioner determines (reg 14(2)(d))`

@export More than one of my active super funds qualifies for the ATO's transfer (s 24NA(3)). Which one must the ATO pay (reg 14)?
GIVEN `the ATO has paid one of them for me this financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the financial year of the transfer, the Commissioner has already paid one or more of those funds for you (a refund of unclaimed, inactive, ERF, voluntary, lost member or temporary resident money, or an earlier transfer)
      `one of them received an amount for me this financial year or last` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of those funds received an amount for you (a contribution or rollover) in this financial year or the one before
      `one of them had the largest balance at the last 30 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of those funds held a larger balance for you than the others at the end of the last completed financial year (no if there was a tie)
GIVETH A `Which of my funds the ATO must pay`
`Which fund must the ATO pay under reg 14` MEANS
    IF `the ATO has paid one of them for me this financial year`
    THEN `the fund the Commissioner has already paid for me this financial year (the most recently paid, if more than one) (reg 14(2)(a))`
    ELSE IF `one of them received an amount for me this financial year or last`
         THEN `the fund that most recently received an amount for me this financial year or last (reg 14(2)(b))`
         ELSE IF `one of them had the largest balance at the last 30 June`
              THEN `the fund with the largest balance for me at the end of the last completed financial year (reg 14(2)(c))`
              ELSE `the fund the Commissioner determines (reg 14(2)(d))`
